From a4d2bec8a2fc437ab98bc0741b6e4261a2cc475e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Noordhuis <info@bnoordhuis.nl>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:50:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] linux: fix value of UV_EFTYPE (#5328)

EFTYPE was never defined on Linux until 7.2. Now that newer kernel
headers define it but older kernel headers don't, we get different
values for UV_EFTYPE depending on where libuv is compiled: -4028 vs.
-134, -136, -169 or -258; the exact value depends on the architecture.

This commit technically breaks ABI because people that compile libuv
against kernel headers will see the value of UV_EFTYPE flip, but since
older kernels don't return the value, and downstream users therefore
are unlikely to actually see or use it, it's probably fine.

The alternative is to remap the new EFTYPE value to the old one
everywhere but that's both a lot of work and it adds overhead.

Fixes: https://github.com/libuv/libuv/issues/5327
---
 include/uv/errno.h | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/uv/errno.h b/include/uv/errno.h
index ac00778cfc5..1727253b844 100644
--- a/include/uv/errno.h
+++ b/include/uv/errno.h
@@ -432,7 +432,16 @@
 # define UV__ENOTTY (-4029)
 #endif
 
-#if defined(EFTYPE) && !defined(_WIN32)
+/* Le sigh. Added in Linux 7.2. */
+#if defined(__linux__) && defined(__hppa__)
+# define UV__EFTYPE (-258)
+#elif defined(__linux__) && defined(__mips__)
+# define UV__EFTYPE (-169)
+#elif defined(__linux__) && defined(__sparc__)
+# define UV__EFTYPE (-136)
+#elif defined(__linux__)
+# define UV__EFTYPE (-134)
+#elif defined(EFTYPE) && !defined(_WIN32)
 # define UV__EFTYPE UV__ERR(EFTYPE)
 #else
 # define UV__EFTYPE (-4028)
